# Dart 3 Updates Rules (from evanca/flutter-ai-rules)

### Branches & Control Flow
1. Use `if-case` statements to match and destructure a value against a single pattern. Example: `if (pair case [int x, int y]) { ... }`.
2. Use `switch` statements to match a value against multiple patterns. Each case body executes without needing `break`.
3. Use `switch` expressions to produce a value based on matching cases. Example:
   ```dart
   final result = switch (state) {
     State.loading => const LoadingWidget(),
     State.success => const SuccessWidget(),
     _ => const ErrorWidget(),
   };
   ```
4. Switch statement/expression must handle all possible values exhaustively. Use `sealed` modifier on classes to enforce compile-time exhaustiveness checking.
5. Add guard clauses to `case` statements using `when`. Example: `case pattern when condition:`.

### Patterns & Destructuring
1. Use wildcard patterns (`_`) to ignore unmatched parts of a value.
2. Destructure records and collections directly:
   ```dart
   var (name, age) = userInfo(json);
   ```
